ned comparison profiles. (2) The oracle is a pinned kernel driver on Lean's checked declaration-admission path (e.g. addDeclCore), not CLI exit status; .olean imports are input artifacts not fresh evidence; elaboration failure ≠ kernel rejection; infer-routine shortcuts forbidden. (3) Fixture = explicit judgment with environment (8-component contract: scope, logical inputs, conversion inputs, provenance, expectations, execution evidence), three task forms (admission, typing, conversion). (4) Unknown is an execution outcome, never a third truth value; harness failures are never negative fixtures. (5) Landing gate: every claimed equivalence fixture matches the pinned oracle; Yin's frozen spec governs Yin correctness — Lean disagreement may be intentional theory difference, not a defect. (6) Corner enumeration follows PHP §4.6: upstream regressions over elaborated dependency closures, one minimal witness per rule, mutations run through the oracle as candidates. Doc deltas: 3 High (:170 comparison profiles + identity-sort boundary fixture; :227 define supported fragment at judgment level; :69 execution contract for \"external oracle\"), 3 Medium, 1 Low, 1 Clarification (Lean stays outside deployed TCB).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14033:Done: (1) Pass 7's two fails were authored-placeholder vs real-PHP mismatches: exc-uncaught-fatal (real PHP reports the uncaught E \"boom\"; the pin said nil) and exc-named-arg-validation-order (the departure target lacked its :zend oracle field). The P4 engineer session hit the claude ACCOUNT rate limit (resets 02:40 - not session-level; a fresh session failed identically), so the seat executed the folds directly per the small-work provision: the uncaught pin authored, the C28 target's :zend added, local three-namespace verify green, committed a18402bc (staged from git status). Pass 8 launched to confirm 0 fails. (2) T3 S4 landed: the instanceof matrix, the Error family (six subclasses + cause/message descriptors), built-in subclassing (e