-error`. The malformed input and host error object are\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:753:Close code `4000`, reason `dao.stream/ended`, maps to `:ws/ended`. Code `4004` is the authoritative not-found close following the disclaimer frame. Code `4002` is a protocol-error teardown. For an established attachment, completion of a 4002 teardown deposits exactly one `:ws/closed` at both the endpoint that initiated the close and the peer that observed it. The detecting endpoint therefore deposits `:ws/error` first and `:ws/closed` when the connection terminates. Before client resolution, closure before `:ws/accept` or `:ws/disclaim` deposits `:ws/transport-error` and then the single `:ws/closed`; after `:ws/disclaim`, it deposits `:ws/not-found` and then `:ws/closed`. Every other peer close or connection loss maps to `:ws/closed` under the exactly-once lifecycle rule.\ndocs/design/adr/0002-share-governed-computation-not-data.md:22:- An always-on accountability floor guarantees immutable provenance of every derivation.\ntest/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc:20:   selected (datomic-q-v1.provenance.edn). Agreement among DaoSpace\ntest/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc:303:    (is (contains-text? (cfx/read-path fx/provenance-path) resource-blake3)\ntest/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc:304:        \"provenance records the same digest\")))\ntest/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc:332:  (let [prov (cfx/read-path fx/provenance-path)]\ntest/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc:335:    (testing \"oracle-executed evidence requires recorded backend provenance\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:190:  \"Collection families and domain metadata, excluding reader provenance.\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2662:   Generated evidence is never their source of truth; provenance is in-file.\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2663:   The file's contract is validated at load: version and provenance are\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:267