ures. It is not a claim of equal implementation cost, nor a proposal to reproduce Lean’s elaborator within that budget.\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:116:Tao extends that retention obligation to written notation: original source bytes and source occurrences remain retrievable after parsing and elaboration. Lowering may omit parentheses, names, or comments from logical term content only because their source representation and provenance remain available.\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:162:The topology follows [row-native macro expansion](./yin.vm.macro.md): transformation between media, ordinary data at boundaries, provenance beside content, and no transformation machinery inside the evaluator. Tao does not automatically reuse the macro expander’s grammar, store, fixpoint rules, or event schema; those contracts address a different transformation.\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:293:## 9. Unitarity and provenance\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:340:A fixed notation can still be misunderstood. V1 narrows the gap between text and explicit term; neither provenance nor a finite fixture suite proves that a human intended the resulting theorem.\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:358:Publishing outputs and provenance follows existing staged-flush and retry contracts. Reuse the macro observer’s operational lessons; do not claim atomicity across independent media unless the composition provides it.\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:366:Two frontends may produce identical term content and different source/provenance records. That is expected. They may also produce different terms from visually similar source; their separate interpretation identities make that difference inspectable.\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:390:- Repeated identical subterms with distinct occurrence provenance.\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:410:- Source and interpretation provenance remain retrievable.\ndocs/design/yang.tao.md:420:Internal syntax objects, helper names, file layout, traversal strategy, and indexing structures are implementation choices. Their observable effects on addresses, binding, diagnostics, or provenance are not.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:287:                                ;   and provenance), K, and nothing to resume into\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:564:exactly as UCF §7.3.2 states, with provenance in a side table outside\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:715: :yin.k/segment  A :yin.k/site n         ; the tail call site, for provenance only\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:844:included, `live` sets and provenance excluded. Of what UCF §7.3 says\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1246:never from provenance or an unavailable AST).\ndocs/design/dao.space.security.md:52:- **Native `m`-provenance.** `yin.vm` maintains the causality graph natively, stamping each output datom with the capability that authorized the continuation. An opaque runtime breaks this chain; an AST evaluator preserves it.\ndocs/design/dao.space.security.md:57:An always-on accountability floor guarantees transparency. The immutable log, combined with `m`-provenance, attributes every authorized computation and every derivation to a specific actor. We rely on **control-as-accountability** in scenarios where control-as-prevention is impossible.\ndocs/design/dao.space.security.md:71:The line that matters is *opaque vs. introspectable `f`*, not *which runtime*. An **opaque** `f` — a raw WASM module or enclave payload with no recoverable AST — is rejected: it forecloses structural policy and breaks `m`-provenance. Running an **introspectable `yin.vm` AST** *via* a TEE, MPC, or FHE is not opaque and is fine; the AST is inspected before it is sealed or compiled.\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:5:Consensus provenance (2026-10-18): gpt-6-astra, author; gemini-4-argon,\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:112:- The October amendments to the register and semantic designs make **A the code identity**. R is the register image checksum. Existing `:hash`, `:image`, and offset rows still use R for native compatibility. Do not publish wasm binaries as a new code