  ;; provenance claims — the roots the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2302:                                  ;; claimed packet's provenance\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:119:**Type:** `:heap` is `{cell-id {:value v :seal s :provenance p}}`; `:gc` is `{:since n :base b :threshold t :pinned #{cell-id}}`\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:123:**Provenance:** an entry may carry an optional private `:provenance` sibling beside `:value` and `:seal`, written only by the privileged mint (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, effect `:cell/new-provenance`) at allocation, never attached, replaced, or cleared afterwards. The VM treats it as opaque data — no frontend dispatch, no reason matching, no rendering — and answers it only through the authenticated private reader (`cell/dsg__provenance`, effect `:cell/provenance`), which returns nil for anything else and is never fatal. `cell/get` returns only `:value`; `cell/set!` and `heap-write` preserve `:provenance` while updating `:value`/`:seal`. The collector traces `:provenance` as data from every live entry, from pinned entries, and as an extra root at allocation, so payload cells referenced only by a retained provenance stay reachable while the wrapper is, and become collectible when the wrapper drops.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:996:- 📖 **Specified elsewhere** - `yin.vm.macro.md` (the expander contract) and `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` §8.4-8.5 (the batch/provenance shape a future expander's events carry).\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:413:(defn new-provenance-cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:415:   `provenance` installed in its private `:provenance` sibling, atomically.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:416:   `provenance` must be non-nil and is otherwise opaque to the VM. Only the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:417:   mint attaches provenance, and only at allocation. Not a guest surface:\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:419:  [value provenance]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:420:  (make-effect :cell/new-provenance {:val value, :provenance provenance}))\nsr