{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | sed -n '375,465p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '2400,2480p;2540,2640p;2760,2855p'\"","aggregated_output":"   375\t;; The `cell` module\n   376\t;; =============================================================================\n   377\t;;\n   378\t;; A cell is a mutable location in the task's `:heap`, reached by a sealed\n   379\t;; `:cell-ref` (Architect cell ruling, slice 1). These are pure effect\n   380\t;; constructors like the stream module's: they touch no heap, and the engine\n   381\t;; interprets the effects they return. The heap is VM state, so a mutation\n   382\t;; is shared by every closure over the ref and is never rolled back when a\n   383\t;; continuation is invoked (box semantics). Beside the three mutators the\n   384\t;; module publishes `authentic?`, the ruling-of-record query a caller's\n   385\t;; compiled code asks the issuer before dereferencing a cell-ref-shaped\n   386\t;; callee; it answers a boolean and changes nothing.\n   387\t\n   388\t(defn new-cell\n   389\t  [v]\n   390\t  (make-effect :cell/new {:val v}))\n   391\t\n   392\t\n   393\t(defn get-cell\n   394\t  [c]\n   395\t  (make-effect :cell/get {:cell c}))\n   396\t\n   397\t\n   398\t(defn set-cell!\n   399\t  [c v]\n   400\t  (make-effect :cell/set! {:cell c, :val v}))\n   401\t\n   402\t\n   403\t(defn authentic-cell?\n   404\t  \"The pure query the cell-ref ruling of record added: does the heap\n   405\t   issue `c` as a cell reference? The engine answers the same\n   406\t   heap+seal predicate `check-ref!` consults, as a boolean, so compiled\n   407\t   call routing can ask the issuer instead of guessing from a value's\n   408\t   shape. Non-fatal, state unchanged.\"\n   409\t  [c]\n   410\t  (make-effect :cell/authentic? {:cell c}))\n   411\t\n   412\t\n   413\t(defn new-provenance-cell\n   414\t  \"The privileged mint: allocate a fresh sealed cell holding `value` with\n   415\t   `provenance` installed in its private `:provenance` sibling, atomically.\n   416\t   `provenance` must be non-nil and is otherwise opaque to the VM. Only the\n   417\t   mint attaches provenance, and only at allocation. Not a guest surface:\n   418\t   the name is compiler-private (`dsg__`).\"\n   419\t  [value provenance]\n   420\t  (make-effect :cell/new-provenance {:val value, :provenance provenance}))\n   421\t\n   422\t\n   423\t(defn provenance-cell\n   424\t  \"The private reader: the `:provenance` a live, authenticated, marked cell\n   425\t   carries, or nil for anything else — an unmarked cell, a forged or dead\n   426\t   reference, or a non-reference. Never fatal, never mutating, and the\n   427\t   engine learns no frontend semantics from the slot. Not a guest surface:\n   428\t   the name is compiler-private (`dsg__`).\"\n   429\t  [candidate]\n   430\t  (make-effect :cell/provenance {:cell candidate}))\n   431\t\n   432\t\n   433\t(def cell-module\n   434\t  \"The `cell` module definition. Registering it is a composition step. The\n   435\t   two `dsg__` bindings are the compiler-private provenance mint and reader:\n   436\t   guest code may neither spell nor construct their names.\"\n   437\t  {'new new-cell, 'get get-cell, 'set! set-cell!, 'authentic? authentic-cell?,\n   438\t   'dsg__new-provenance new-provenance-cell,\n   439\t   'dsg__provenance provenance-cell})\n   440\t\n   441\t\n   442\t(def cell-profiles\n   443\t  \"UCF 7.5.2 profiles for the `cell` module's bindings: each an\n   444\t   `:effectful` pure effect constructor declaring its one effect kind.\"\n   445\t  {'new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :effectful [1] #{:cell/new} :none)\n   446\t   'get (vm/primitive-profile 'get :effectful [1] #{:cell/get} :none)\n   447\t   'set! (vm/primitive-profile 'set! :effectful [2] #{:cell/set!} :none)\n   448\t   'authentic? (vm/primitive-profile 'authentic? :effectful [1]\n   449\t                                     #{:cell/authentic?} :none)\n   450\t   'dsg__new-provenance (vm/primitive-profile 'dsg__new-provenance\n   451\t                                              :effectful [2]\n   452\t                                              #{:cell/new-provenance} :none)\n   453\t   'dsg__provenance (vm/primitive-profile 'dsg__provenance\n   454\t                                          :effectful [1]\n   455\t                                          #{:cell/provenance} :none)})\n   456\t\n   457\t\n   458\t(defn register-cell-module\n   459\t  \"Return registry with the `cell` module registered.\"\n   460\t  [registry]\n   461\t  (register-host-module registry 'cell cell-module cell-profiles))\n   462\t\n   463\t\n   464\t;; =============================================================================\n   465\t;; Built-in effect handlers\n  2400\t    {:state (:state result), :value (:value result), :blocked? false}))\n  2401\t\n  2402\t\n  2403\t(defn- with-primitive-effects\n  2404\t  \"`state` whose `:callable-effects` index was built from its current\n  2405\t   `:primitives` map: the held index when that map is `identical?` to\n  2406\t   the one it was built from, else a rebuilt one.\"\n  2407\t  [state]\n  2408\t  (let [primitives (:primitives state)]\n  2409\t    (if (identical? primitives (:primitives (:callable-effects state)))\n  2410\t      state\n  2411\t      (assoc state\n  2412\t             :callable-effects\n  2413\t             (vm/primitive-effects-index primitives\n  2414\t                                         (:primitive-profiles state))))))\n  2415\t\n  2416\t\n  2417\t(defn check-callee-effect!\n  2418\t  \"Refuse `effect`, the result of applying host callable `f`, when `f`\n  2419\t   carries a profile whose declared effect set lacks the effect's kind\n  2420\t   (D4, layered on the host type). `f`'s declared set is the union of\n  2421\t   its primitive and module declarations, read from identity-keyed\n  2422\t   indexes: the VM's `:callable-effects`, rebuilt here when `:primitives`\n  2423\t   changed since it was built, and the registry's, which\n  2424\t   `module/register-host-module` maintains. The check runs only on an\n  2425\t   effect result and costs nothing on an ordinary call. A callable with\n  2426\t   no profile is the composition's trusted value and passes. Returns\n  2427\t   `state`, carrying the index it checked against, for the caller to\n  2428\t   dispatch the effect on.\"\n  2429\t  [state f effect]\n  2430\t  (let [state (with-primitive-effects state)\n  2431\t        from-primitives (get (:index (:callable-effects state)) f)\n  2432\t        from-modules (get (:callable-effects (:modules state)) f)\n  2433\t        declared (if (and from-primitives from-modules)\n  2434\t                   (into from-primitives from-modules)\n  2435\t                   (or from-primitives from-modules))]\n  2436\t    (if (and declared (not (contains? declared (:effect effect))))\n  2437\t      (fail \"Effect outside the callee's declared profile\"\n  2438\t            {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undeclared-effect,\n  2439\t             :yin.k/effect (:effect effect),\n  2440\t             :yin.k/effects declared})\n  2441\t      state)))\n  2442\t\n  2443\t\n  2444\t(defn- heap-write\n  2445\t  \"`state` with heap cell `id` holding `v` under `seal`: allocation when the\n  2446\t   cell is new, a write (the seal unchanged) when it is live. A write\n  2447\t   preserves the entry's `:provenance` sibling; only the mint attaches one,\n  2448\t   and only at allocation.\"\n  2449\t  [state id seal v]\n  2450\t  (update-in state [:heap id] (fn [entry] (assoc entry :value v, :seal seal))))\n  2451\t\n  2452\t\n  2453\t;; =============================================================================\n  2454\t;; Heap reclamation (Architect heap-reclamation design, slice 1)\n  2455\t;; =============================================================================\n  2456\t;;\n  2457\t;; A deterministic, allocation-triggered, stop-the-world mark-sweep over\n  2458\t;; `:heap`, as a pure `vm -> vm'`. The `:cell/new` arm counts allocations in\n  2459\t;; `:gc` and collects when the count reaches the threshold, so two runs\n  2460\t;; collect at the same allocation. Marking runs over the heap as it was when\n  2461\t;; the cycle began (a persistent map, so the snapshot is a reference) and the\n  2462\t;; sweep removes only ids of that snapshot: an id allocated at or after the\n  2463\t;; cycle's counter start is not in it and is spared. A budgeted marker can\n  2464\t;; later run the same `trace` k steps per round. Ids are never reused:\n  2465\t;; `:id-counter` only grows, so a ref to a swept cell names nothing and is\n  2466\t;; refused `:dead-or-forged-reference`.\n  2467\t\n  2468\t(defn- heap-ref-id\n  2469\t  \"The id the map `x` names when it is a `:cell-ref` authentic against\n  2470\t   `heap`, else nil.\"\n  2471\t  [heap x]\n  2472\t  (when (= :cell-ref (:type x))\n  2473\t    (let [id (:id x)\n  2474\t          entry (get heap id)]\n  2475\t      (when (and (some? entry) (= (:seal x) (:seal entry))) id))))\n  2476\t\n  2477\t\n  2478\t(defn- moded\n  2479\t  \"`work` with each of `xs` pushed in `mode`, `:kernel` or `:data`.\"\n  2480\t  [work mode xs]\n  2540\t     table entry, a closure or continuation payload, or a kernel child of\n  2541\t     one): the kernel's `gc-children` may interpret it, and answers which\n  2542\t     of its children are kernel positions and which are values. A value\n  2543\t     it does not recognize is walked whole, as data.\n  2544\t   - `:data`, a value position (an environment value, an operand, a\n  2545\t     register, a cell's content): every map is walked whole, never\n  2546\t     pruned, so a guest map shaped like a frame cannot hide a cell ref.\n  2547\t     Only a closure or continuation, a host type no guest can forge,\n  2548\t     re-enters `:kernel` mode through its payload.\n  2549\t\n  2550\t   Scalars hold nothing. With `follow?` a newly found id's content is\n  2551\t   traced too, as data (marking); without, only the refs met directly\n  2552\t   (pinning). Each object is visited once per mode, so shared environments\n  2553\t   cost one walk and a cell holding its own ref terminates; the visit is\n  2554\t   keyed on identity (`Visited`), never on a value's structural hash,\n  2555\t   which for a closure or a continuation would recurse through the whole\n  2556\t   chain it holds. The worklist is explicit: a deep continuation chain\n  2557\t   does not grow the host stack.\"\n  2558\t  [vm heap roots found follow?]\n  2559\t  (let [children-of (if (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\n  2560\t                      #(module/gc-children vm %)\n  2561\t                      (constantly nil))]\n  2562\t    (loop [work (-> ()\n  2563\t                    (moded :kernel (:kernel roots))\n  2564\t                    (moded :data (:data roots)))\n  2565\t           seen #{}\n  2566\t           found found]\n  2567\t      (if (empty? work)\n  2568\t        found\n  2569\t        (let [[mode x] (peek work)\n  2570\t              work (pop work)\n  2571\t              visit (when-not (scalar? x) (Visited. mode x))]\n  2572\t          (if (or (nil? visit) (contains? seen visit))\n  2573\t            (recur work seen found)\n  2574\t            (let [id (when (map? x) (heap-ref-id heap x))\n  2575\t                  new-id? (and (some? id) (not (contains? found id)))\n  2576\t                  children (when (and (= :kernel mode)\n  2577\t                                      (not (values/host-typed? x)))\n  2578\t                             (children-of x))\n  2579\t                  work (cond-> work\n  2580\t                         (and new-id? follow?)\n  2581\t                         (-> (conj [:data (:value (get heap id))])\n  2582\t                             (conj [:data (:provenance (get heap id))]))\n  2583\t                         (values/host-typed? x)\n  2584\t                         (conj [:kernel (values/payload x)])\n  2585\t                         (some? children)\n  2586\t                         (-> (moded :kernel (:kernel children))\n  2587\t                             (moded :data (:values children)))\n  2588\t                         (and (nil? children) (map? x))\n  2589\t                         (-> (moded :data (keys x))\n  2590\t                             (moded :data (vals x)))\n  2591\t                         (and (nil? children) (not (map? x)) (coll? x))\n  2592\t                         (moded :data x))]\n  2593\t              (recur work\n  2594\t                     (conj seen visit)\n  2595\t                     (if new-id? (conj found id) found)))))))))\n  2596\t\n  2597\t\n  2598\t(defn- gc-roots\n  2599\t  \"Every root of `vm` (design Q1), by mode: the kernel's registers as it\n  2600\t   classifies them (`module/gc-roots`), each entry of `:parked`,\n  2601\t   `:wait-set` and `:ready-queue` as a kernel position, the store and\n  2602\t   every module store as values, then `extra` as values. Code, images,\n  2603\t   the registry, primitives, `:callable-effects`, telemetry and\n  2604\t   `:resources` are not roots: a literal can never be an authentic ref,\n  2605\t   and a value inside a stream is the medium's (hence pinning).\"\n  2606\t  [vm extra]\n  2607\t  (let [kernel (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\n  2608\t                 (module/gc-roots vm))]\n  2609\t    {:kernel (-> (vec (:kernel kernel))\n  2610\t                 (into (vals (:parked vm)))\n  2611\t                 (into (:wait-set vm))\n  2612\t                 (into (:ready-queue vm))),\n  2613\t     :data (-> [(:store vm) (:module-stores vm)]\n  2614\t               (into (:values kernel))\n  2615\t               (into extra))}))\n  2616\t\n  2617\t\n  2618\t(defn- mark\n  2619\t  \"The ids of `heap` live from `roots` and from the `pinned` ids: a pinned\n  2620\t   cell is a root, so its content — value and provenance — is traced too,\n  2621\t   as data.\"\n  2622\t  [vm heap roots pinned]\n  2623\t  (let [pins (filterv #(contains? heap %) pinned)]\n  2624\t    (trace vm\n  2625\t           heap\n  2626\t           (update roots :data\n  2627\t                   into (mapcat (fn [id] (let [e (get heap id)]\n  2628\t                                           [(:value e) (:provenance e)]))\n  2629\t                                pins))\n  2630\t           (set pins)\n  2631\t           true)))\n  2632\t\n  2633\t\n  2634\t(defn- sweep\n  2635\t  \"`heap` without each id of the cycle's `snapshot` that `marked` lacks.\n  2636\t   An id allocated after the snapshot is not in it, so it is spared.\"\n  2637\t  [heap snapshot marked]\n  2638\t  (reduce-kv (fn [h id _] (if (contains? marked id) h (dissoc h id)))\n  2639\t             heap\n  2640\t             snapshot))\n  2760\t            (if (and (:park result) (= :running (vm/gate-mode state)))\n  2761\t              (let [builder (or (get park-entry-fns :stream/poll)\n  2762\t                                (get park-entry-fns :stream/next))\n  2763\t                    built (when builder (builder state effect result))]\n  2764\t                (handle-stream-block\n  2765\t                  result\n  2766\t                  (when built\n  2767\t                    (assoc built\n  2768\t                           :reason :observe\n  2769\t                           :op :poll\n  2770\t                           :cursor-ref (:cursor-ref result)\n  2771\t                           :stream-id (:stream-id result)))))\n  2772\t              {:state (:state result),\n  2773\t               :value (:value result),\n  2774\t               :blocked? false}))\n  2775\t          :stream/close\n  2776\t          (let [_ (gate-refuse! state effect)\n  2777\t                close-result (handle-close state effect)]\n  2778\t            {:state (:state close-result), :value nil, :blocked? false})\n  2779\t          ;; `:heap` is VM state, not continuation state: a write is seen\n  2780\t          ;; by every holder of the ref and survives continuation invocation\n  2781\t          :cell/new\n  2782\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym (count-allocation state (:val effect)) \"cell\")\n  2783\t                ref (issue-ref s' :cell-ref id)]\n  2784\t            {:state (heap-write s' id (:seal ref) (:val effect)),\n  2785\t             :value ref,\n  2786\t             :blocked? false})\n  2787\t          :cell/get\n  2788\t          (let [id (check-ref! state :cell/get :cell-ref (:cell effect))]\n  2789\t            ;; the content is answered as data, never re-interpreted\n  2790\t            {:state state,\n  2791\t             :value (get-in state [:heap id :value]),\n  2792\t             :blocked? false})\n  2793\t          :cell/set!\n  2794\t          (let [id (check-ref! state :cell/set! :cell-ref (:cell effect))]\n  2795\t            {:state (heap-write state id (get-in state [:heap id :seal])\n  2796\t                                (:val effect)),\n  2797\t             :value (:val effect),\n  2798\t             :blocked? false})\n  2799\t          ;; The cell-ref ruling of record: the same heap+seal predicate\n  2800\t          ;; `check-ref!` consults (r10), answered as data instead of\n  2801\t          ;; failing closed, so compiled call routing can ask the issuer\n  2802\t          ;; whether it issued a reference. A pure query: no state change,\n  2803\t          ;; never fatal, and the engine learns no frontend semantics.\n  2804\t          :cell/authentic?\n  2805\t          {:state state,\n  2806\t           :value (authentic-ref? state :cell-ref (:cell effect)),\n  2807\t           :blocked? false}\n  2808\t          ;; The privileged mint: a fresh sealed cell with `:value` and a\n  2809\t          ;; private `:provenance` sibling installed atomically. Provenance\n  2810\t          ;; is opaque to the engine; it is answered only by `:cell/provenance`.\n  2811\t          :cell/new-provenance\n  2812\t          (let [_ (when (nil? (:provenance effect))\n  2813\t                    (fail \"Provenance mint refuses nil provenance\"\n  2814\t                          {:reason :nil-provenance, :effect :cell/new-provenance}))\n  2815\t                [id s'] (gensym (count-allocation state\n  2816\t                                                  (:val effect)\n  2817\t                                                  (:provenance effect))\n  2818\t                                \"cell\")\n  2819\t                ref (issue-ref s' :cell-ref id)]\n  2820\t            {:state (assoc-in s' [:heap id] {:value (:val effect),\n  2821\t                                             :seal (:seal ref),\n  2822\t                                             :provenance (:provenance effect)}),\n  2823\t             :value ref,\n  2824\t             :blocked? false})\n  2825\t          ;; The private reader: authenticate before consulting the slot, so\n  2826\t          ;; an unauthenticated candidate answers nil instead of refusing.\n  2827\t          ;; Never fatal, never mutating.\n  2828\t          :cell/provenance\n  2829\t          (let [ref (:cell effect)]\n  2830\t            {:state state,\n  2831\t             :value (when (authentic-ref? state :cell-ref ref)\n  2832\t                      (get-in state [:heap (:id ref) :provenance])),\n  2833\t             :blocked? false})\n  2834\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"effect\")\n  2835\t                handler (module/get-effect-handler (:modules state)\n  2836\t                                                   (:effect effect))]\n  2837\t            (if handler\n  2838\t              (handler s' effect (assoc opts :id id))\n  2839\t              (fail \"Unknown effect\" {:effect (:effect effect)}))))]\n  2840\t    (update result\n  2841\t            :state\n  2842\t            (fn [result-state]\n  2843\t              (telemetry/emit-snapshot (assoc result-state\n  2844\t                                              :value (:value result))\n  2845\t                                       :effect\n  2846\t                                       {:effect-type (:effect effect)})))))\n  2847\t\n  2848\t\n  2849\t;; =============================================================================\n  2850\t;; Program Cache Machinery\n  2851\t;; =============================================================================\n  2852\t\n  2853\t(def default-compiled-cache-limit 8)\n  2854\t\n  2855\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
