{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat ../datomworld-r3-orch/.git; rg -n 'defn- call-entry|defn- compile-guest-call|raise-exit|condition|clj/raise|call-token' ../datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | head -95; nl -ba ../datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | sed -n '80,255p'; nl -ba ../datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '1320,1450p'\"","aggregated_output":"gitdir: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.git/worktrees/datomworld-r3-orch\n846:;; guest call delivers an escaping condition through the §8.10.7 raise exit.\n887:;; plain values. A guest call delivers a callee's escaping condition through\n889:;; The caught value IS the payload/condition — no wrapper, no retention\n901:   `clj/raise` delivers to, a `:finally` frame a one-argument thunk every\n918:    [clj/raise\n924:             (do (clj/pop-frame hs) ((dsg__get hs 1) e) (clj/raise e))\n926:    [clj/throw (fn [e] (clj/raise e))]\n979:   condition's wrapper carries the original payload privately, so\n1178:(defn- call-entry\n1205:        ;; :yang.call/thrown condition to the caller's raise exit.\n1382:(defn- compile-guest-call\n1384:   the callee's escaping condition into the clj continuation: a\n1385:   `:yang.call/thrown` condition delivers its payload (the caught value IS the\n1386:   payload), any other value (a qualified protocol condition or an unmarked\n1395:          condition (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"condition\"))\n1396:          raise-exit (u/lam [condition]\n1397:                            (assoc (u/app (u/v 'clj/raise)\n1400:                                                   (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v condition)\n1403:                                            (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v condition)\n1405:                                            (u/v condition)))\n1408:                             (u/lit []) raise-exit)\n1409:          refused (u/app (u/v 'clj/raise)\n1410:                         (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/condition)\n1424:                            raise-exit)\n1513:                                       (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/condition)\n1599:  \"Compile a conditional (if) expression to Universal AST.\n2378:                                             '(clj/raise\n2379:                                                (yang.call/condition\n2394:           ;; `clj/raise`, ...) is the port's `%capture` handler-stack scheme,\n2577:        ;; This is a SOURCE-LEVEL throw of an UNMARKED condition-shaped map\n2580:        ;; :yang.call/thrown condition and authenticates THAT outer condition\n2584:        :else (throw (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable {:yang.call/callee f}))))\n3017:   inside the unit thunk is conditional to the linker, so no body read\n    80\t       (do (cell/set! clj.rt/globals\n    81\t                      (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name value))\n    82\t           value))]\n    83\t    [clj/global-get\n    84\t     (fn [name]\n    85\t       (if (data/contains? (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n    86\t         (get (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n    87\t         :clj/unbound))]\n    88\t\n    89\t    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- escapes\n    90\t    ;; The continuation family, mirroring py/ts/php (their preludes are the\n    91\t    ;; reference implementations): the dynamic context is one record in one\n    92\t    ;; cell, `clj.rt/ctx`, holding {:handlers} — clojure has no generators,\n    93\t    ;; no `with` managers and no recursion-limit hook, so there is no\n    94\t    ;; :depth/:base/:frame accounting the way py/php carry it. The handler\n    95\t    ;; stack is a chain of frames [tag payload rest n]: a :handler frame\n    96\t    ;; holds the continuation `throw` delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk\n    97\t    ;; of one argument (the thrown value, or nil) that every exit through\n    98\t    ;; it runs; n, the frame count, makes \"unwind to here\"