patches), `bb563fe1` (pins), `0f0ab852` (forgery contract pins),\n    13\t`00ca2d1c` (the adoption), `428bbdd7` (scanner-pin regeneration). The other span content\n    14\t(VM provenance primitive ff8b980a/566c5450/50c9485a, JS R1+R3, clojure cc2, PHP Round C)\n    15\tbelongs to arcs with their own reviews and is treated as landed context, re-consulted only\n    16\twhere the adoption depends on it.\n    17\t\n    18\t## Per-question verdicts\n    19\t\n    20\t**Q1 — Provenance wiring correctness: PASS.**\n    21\t- Mint: `dsg__condition-exception` (prelude.cljc:1044-1053) mints through\n    22\t  `cell/dsg__new-provenance` with the complete original condition — both call sites\n    23\t  (prelude.cljc:1074-1076 R2 ForeignException wrap, :1078-1080 R3 TypeError wrap) pass the\n    24\t  entire condition map delivered by the raise continuation, reason and payload included.\n    25\t- Egress: the single boundary exit (`py/function-entry`, prelude.cljc:918) reads\n    26\t  `(cell/dsg__provenance e)` before any forwarding decision; `nil?` → the plain fresh\n    27\t  `:yang.call/thrown` with the value as payload. The engine reader authenticates first\n    28\t  (engine.cljc:2828-2833: `authentic-ref?` — heap+seal) and answers nil for forged refs,\n    29\t  dead ids, and non-refs — never fatal. `nil` ⇔ unmarked is sound because the mint refuses\n    30\t  nil provenance (engine.cljc:2812-2814), so a marked cell always answers non-nil.\n    31\t- No `:py/retained-condition` authority reads remain anywhere in python src — the only\n    32\t  occurrences are the guest-side attack strings in the forgery pins\n    33\t  (python_exception_test.clj:112-115) and the grandfathered TypeScript surface.\n    34\t- The two remaining raise-exit calls (prelude.cljc:901, :903) deliver freshly constructed\n    35\t  protocol refusals of the invocation itself before any body runs — correctly not\n    36\t  provenance-authenticated. `py/function-entry` is the only `:yang.call/entry` installer in\n    37\t  the prelude (prelude.cljc:935); there is no second egress.\n    38\t\n    39\t**Q2 — R2 lifetime rules: PASS on every clause.**\n    40\t- Identity-owned: provenance is the private `:provenance` heap sibling, installed only at\n    41\t  allocation (engine.cljc:2811-2824); no content key is consulted.\n    42\t- Outside source-writable attributes: `py/setattr` writes `:attrs` inside the content map\n    43\t  via `cell/set!`; `heap-write` preserves the sibling (engine.cljc:2444-2450). The\n    44\t  overwrite pin (python-retained-overwrite-test) exercises exactly this and the original\n    45\t  condition still forwards.\n    46\t- No ambient registry: nothing registered anywhere; the state rides the heap entry, traced\n    47\t  by GC together with the value (engine.cljc:2580-2582, 2626-2629), so reachability of the\n    48\t  exception retains the whole condition/payload cluster and dropping it reclaims both.\n    49\t- Wrapper non-stacking: an already-local BaseException instance is re-raised raw\n    50\t  (prelude.cljc:1067-1071); only otherwise-foreign payloads wrap, once, at reception; the\n    51\t  unchanged rethrow forwards the original condition at egress, so no ForeignException ever\n    52\t  contains another and repeated crossings never accumulate wrappers.\n    53\t- Formatting never invokes foreign methods: the ForeignException is a locally generated\n    54\t  class (fixed local message \"foreign exception\"); typed catches match the local hierarchy\n    55\t  (`py.b/Exception` base), never guessed foreign names.\n    56\t\n    57\t**Q3 — Export/alias audit (the sol-named risk): PASS.**\n    58\tVerified statically, the python twin of the js exported-helper class does not exist:\n    59\t- `core/exports` (yang/core/prelude.cljc:71-76) keeps only keys in namespace `py`;\n    60\t  `dsg__condition-exception` is a bare symbol → not in `module-exports`. Nothing else in\n    61\t  the prelude wraps the mint — exactly four `dsg__` occurrences in the whole python tree\n    62\t  (host-names declaration, egress read, mint def, its two call sites).\n    63\t- Guest python source cannot spell the names lexically (`-`/`/` are not identifier\n    64\t  characters); guest Clojure source is refused by the reserved-prefix checks in any role —\n    65\t  definition target and binder at yang/clojure.cljc:424-446, variable/binder/store-key/\n    66\t  definition-key at the shared row admission (yin/vm/macro.cljc:586-644), with the\n    67\t  exported-helper (yin/variable, yin/lambda, yin/make-def) and macro-assembly routes\n    68\t  pinned at the VM level (provenance_test.cljc:245-322).\n    69\t- No dict exposure: the builtins dict is populated only from `builtin-classes`/\n    70\t  `builtin-functions`/`method-implementations` (prelude.cljc:3626-3640) — none mention the\n    71\t  mint or the doors; `runtime-keys` (prelude.cljc:3705-3712) is likewise clean. The py\n    72\t  prelude module is a linker module, never a `py/module-run` object, so it is not in\n    73\t  `sys.modules` and has no `__dict__` to enumerate; guest module dicts hold only what\n    74\t  guest bodies define. `host-names` requiring the two doors is a composition-time\n    75\t  requirement (fail-closed direction), not an exposure.\n    76\t- The exported `py/call-kw` reaches the mint only with conditions the runtime itself\n    77\t  constructed from genuine foreign invocations — provenance-by-construction, not\n    78\t  attacker-chosen.\n    79\t\n    80\t**Q4 — Test weakening: PASS.**\n    81\t- `test/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj`: +125/−0 across the entire span — purely\n    82\t  additive. `exception_contract.clj` changed one js guest fixture line (`saved = e` →\n    83\t  `globalThis.saved = e` — a repair of the retain fixture, strengthening it);\n    84\t  `exception_contract_test.clj` additions only. No python fixture expected-value changed.\n    85\t- Deletion-heavy files in the span (programs_p5b2.cljc, float_addre