with valid-invocation? condition\n   155\t     thrown transfer invoke invoke-with})\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(def uast\n   159\t  \"The bundled definitions, in source order and tail marked.\"\n   160\t  (u/mark-tails\n   161\t    (reduce (fn [ast [key form]]\n   162\t              (u/then ast (u/def! key (u/sexp->uast form))))\n   163\t            (u/def! (ffirst definitions)\n   164\t                    (u/sexp->uast (second (first definitions))))\n   165\t            (rest definitions))))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t(def module-uast\n   169\t  \"The linked module tree built from the same `definitions`. C1\n   170\t   finalized, like every published production tree: its\n   171\t   `:yang/call-site` markers publish beside its manifest (see\n   172\t   `yin.vm.linker.publish`).\"\n   173\t  (let [stripped (core/module-definitions \"yang.call\" :yang.call/uninit\n   174\t                                          [] definitions)]\n   175\t    (u/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree stripped []))))\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t(def module-exports\n   179\t  \"Public module exports (private helper definitions stay internal).\"\n   180\t  public-exports)\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\t(def ^:private module-free-names\n   184\t  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n   185\t\n   186\t\n   187\t(defn module-spec\n   188\t  \"The linker module spec for `yang.call` over `registry`.\"\n   189\t  [registry]\n   190\t  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name\n   191\t                     :ast module-uast\n   192\t                     :exports module-exports\n   193\t                     :requires {}\n   194\t                     :free-names module-free-names\n   195\t                     :registry registry\n   196\t                     :message \"the yang.call module reads an undeclared name\"\n   197\t                     :refusal-ns \"yang.call\"}))\n  3835\tremain refused. Live closures in an invocation must not be placed in\n  3836\tcanonical literal data or sent as a purported portable request.\n  3837\t\n  3838\t#### 8.10.7 Normal return and escaping conditions\n  3839\t\n  3840\tNormal return is the value of ordinary Yin application. There is no\n  3841\textra return continuation, completion packet around each result, or new\n  3842\tlanguage-specific return instruction.\n  3843\t\n  3844\tAn escaping source exception invokes the supplied raise exit with:\n  3845\t\n  3846\t```clojure\n  3847\t{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n  3848\t :yang.call/value  original-thrown-value}\n  3849\t```\n  3850\t\n  3851\tThis is the argument to an exceptional continuation transfer, not an\n  3852\tordinary return. Returning an identical-looking map returns normal data.\n  3853\tLikewise, a source program throwing a map with these keys throws that\n  3854\tmap as the **payload of a new condition**; its shape is never evidence\n  3855\tthat it is already a condition to forward. No engine-effect value is\n  3856\tsynthesized.\n  3857\t\n  3858\tProtocol failures use qualified reasons such as\n  3859\t`:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`, and\n  3860\t`:yang.call/unsupported-binding`, with plain evidence. The caller maps\n  3861\tthem to a documented local exception form retaining the complete\n  3862\toriginal condition. Callee argument-binding failures retain the actual\n  3863\tcallee exception under `:yang.call/thrown`. These reasons do not extend\n  3864\t`dao.stream`'s outcome algebra.\n  3865\t\n  3866\tThe receiving caller interprets an escaping exception as follows:\n  3867\t\n  3868\t1. A payload valid as an exception in its own runtime retains that\n  3869\t   runtime's ordinary catching and identity behavior.\n  3870\t2. A runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values, such as JavaScript,\n  3871\t   may deliver the original payload directly.\n  3872\t3. A runtime requiring exception objects, such as Python or PHP,\n  3873\t   represents an otherwise foreign payload with its own\n  3874\t   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\n  3875\t   payload. Catch-all catches this local object. Typed source catches\n  3876\t   match its local hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names.\n  3877\t\n  3878\t`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\n  3879\tUnchanged rethrow propagates the original condition without adding\n  3880\twrappers. Raising a new exception creates a new condition. Crossing back\n  3881\tinto a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original\n  3882\ttype and identity. Formatting a foreign payload must not implicitly\n  3883\tinvoke a foreign method.\n  3884\t\n  3885\tThe runtime associates its generated wrapper's identity with the retained\n  3886\tcondition for the wrapper's entire lifetime, separate from source-writable\n  3887\tattributes. The association normally lives in private wrapper-cell\n  3888\tcontents, or an equivalent task-owned identity structure with the same\n  3889\tlifetime. It survives storing or returning the wrapper after the creating\n  3890\tcall/catch activation has ended, and remains recoverable when that same\n  3891\twrapper is rethrown in another activation. Temporary catch state alone is\n  3892\tinsufficient. Reachability/reclamation must retain the condition and its\n  3893\tpayload while the wrapper is live, without an ambient registry.\n  3894\t\n  3895\tThe runtime must not detect wrappers or unwrap arbitrary maps by their\n  3896\tkey names. JavaScript may expose raw payloads for\n  3897\t`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\n  3898\tretain that failure's qualified condition. Rethrowing the same generated\n  3899\texception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\n  3900\tthrowing an unrelated value creates a new `:yang.call/thrown` condition.\n  3901\tSaved activation state refers to this identity-owned association; exiting\n  3902\tor restoring a catch does not destroy it.\n  3903\t\n  3904\tVM application/custody defects and host implementation failures remain\n  3905\toperational failures. Do not catch them broadly and relabel them as\n  3906\tsource exceptions. Existing explicit stream/module refusals keep their\n  3907\tsource mappings under the relevant profiles.\n  3908\t\n  3909\t#### 8.10.8 Cleanup, re-entry, and suspension\n  3910\t\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-eZmQW3AR' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-13 05:41:05.273 xcodebuild[27179:127180142]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-13 05:41:05.773 xcodebuild[27179:127180135] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-UtwnEk1h' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-13 05:41:07.546 xcodebuild[27190:127180239]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-13 05:41:07.974 xcodebuild[27190:127180237] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ncommit 00ca2d1cb6bcf53a3a68872ad2021b7ef8516de6\nAuthor:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nAuthorDate: Thu Nov 12 02:46:37 2026 +0700\nCommit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nCommitDate: Thu Nov 12 02:46:37 2026 +0700\n\n    feat(python): wire wrapper mint/read onto the VM provenance primitive\n    \n    Adopt the landed provenance primitive (cell/dsg__new-provenance /\n    cell/dsg__provenance) for Python's generated-exception retention, retiring\n    the forgeable :py/retained-condition visible-slot stamp.\n    \n    - Mint: py/condition-exception -> dsg__condition-exception, minting through\n      cell/dsg__new-provenance so the complete original condition rides the\n      private :provenance heap sibling, installed atomically at allocation.\n    - Read: the :917 egress authenticates through cell/dsg__provenance; nil ->\n      the plain fresh :yang.call/thrown path.\n    - Remove :py/retained-condition as an authority source (the key writes and\n      the slot read are gone); guest-visible wrapper writes stay legal and\n      cannot touch provenance (heap-write preserves the sibling).\n    - Export audit: dsg__condition-exception is a compiler-private (dsg__) bare\n      name, outside the py/ export list, projections and aliases, so no guest\n      can mint arbitrary provenance through it.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc | 41 ++++++++++++++-------------------\n 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
