{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba r3-fix-wt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '912,1005p'; nl -ba ../datomworld-r3-orch/test/yang/clojure_test.clj | sed -n '1815,1895p'; rg -n 'protocol|observation|ex-data|shape' ../datomworld-r3-orch/test/yang/clojure_test.clj | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"   912\t;; the payload and every guest observation (equality in any position, map\n   913\t;; keys, count, assoc, truthiness, predicates under any spelling, passage\n   914\t;; to another unit) is correct by construction, with no compiler routing.\n   915\t;; No wrapper, no retention: the wire condition is reconstructible from\n   916\t;; the payload as a fresh `:yang.call/thrown` at the public boundary.\n   917\t;;\n   918\t;; The wrapper survives ONLY as clojure's documented local form for\n   919\t;; QUALIFIED protocol conditions (`:yang.call/not-callable`,\n   920\t;; `:invalid-invocation`, `:unsupported-binding`): a task-owned cell whose\n   921\t;; contents are [visible condition], minted through the issuer-only\n   922\t;; retained mint (`cell/dsg__new-retained`, a name guest source cannot\n   923\t;; spell). Retention is bound to heap identity, not contents: the engine\n   924\t;; marks the wrapper's heap entry `:retained`, `cell/set!` refuses marked\n   925\t;; entries (contents frozen for the wrapper's lifetime), and the pure\n   926\t;; `cell/retained?` query answers from the heap, so a guest copy of the\n   927\t;; contents in a fresh cell decodes as an ordinary payload, never as a\n   928\t;; retained condition. The association is the cell's identity, so saving\n   929\t;; and returning the wrapper works, and so does a rethrow from another\n   930\t;; activation. Decoding reads cell contents and never applies a guest\n   931\t;; value.\n   932\t\n   933\t(def ^:private visible-of-form\n   934\t  '(fn [dsg__value]\n   935\t     (if (data/map? dsg__value)\n   936\t       (let [dsg__decoded